aasjournalv7.1.bst -- AAS journal BibTeX style
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Derived from Patrick W. Daly's natbib/custom-bib styles and revised by Amy
Hendrickson and Aptara for the AAS journals. The file carries this notice
verbatim:

    NOTICE:
    This file may be used for non-profit purposes.
    It may not be distributed in exchange for money,
      other than distribution costs.

    The author provides it `as is' and does not guarantee it in any way.

    Copyright (C) 1994-98 Patrick W. Daly

Note that this is a non-commercial restriction and therefore not an
open-source license. It is reproduced here rather than overridden.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
orcid-ID.png -- ORCID iD icon
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ships with the AASTeX distribution and is loaded by aastex702.cls to render the
icon beside author names. The ORCID iD icon is a mark of ORCID, Inc.; its use is
governed by ORCID's trademark and brand guidelines, https://orcid.org/trademark-and-id-display-guidelines
